<title>USA: NeoPath gets microscopic imaging patent.</title>
<headline>NeoPath gets microscopic imaging patent.</headline>
<dateline>REDMOND, Wash. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>NeoPath Inc said on Friday that the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office will grant a new patent for technology the company has developed for microscopic imaging.</p>
<p>NeoPath said it is currently using the invention in the AutoPap 300 QC System, its automated device for rescreening Pap smear slides for abnormal cervical cells.</p>
<p>Company officials did not return calls for further information.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
